  "details": "YouTube Live is not working.\nNormal YouTube videos can be played correctly.\nTherefore, there might be some issue with VRC_SyncVideoStream and YouTube Live.\n\nThis is my output_log.txt:\n\n(1)2019.01.16 02:50:10 Log        -  [VRC_TriggerInternal] 632.9056 SyncType_LiveStream via OnInteract executing [SendRPC (False, 0.000, 2, \"StreamParent\", SetSyncType, 147)]\n(2)2019.01.16 02:50:10 Log        -  [Network Processing] RPC invoked SetSyncType on StreamParent for sunasaji\n(3)2019.01.16 02:50:14 Log        -  [VRC_TriggerInternal] 636.2822 NextButton via OnInteract executing [SendRPC (False, 0.000, 2, \"StreamParent\", Next, 0)]\n(4)2019.01.16 02:50:14 Log        -  [Network Processing] RPC invoked Next on StreamParent for sunasaji\n(5)2019.01.16 02:50:14 Log        -  StreamParent play index: 11\n(6)2019.01.16 02:51:06 Log        -  [VRC_TriggerInternal] 688.8391 PrevButton via OnInteract executing [SendRPC (False, 0.000, 2, \"StreamParent\", Previous, 0)]\n\n(1)-(2): I set \"SyncType\" to \"Livestream\"\n(3)-(5): I pressed \"Next\" button and play index:11 (Live URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bszm6XDdygY)\nBut the stream is not played, video screen remains black.\n\nAnd I tried to use YouTube Live streaming in some worlds, such as \"Movie Theater 3D 16x9\" or \"Tsubokura's Home\" or \"Cinema Home In Space\".\nThen, all of them could not play YouTube Live, but can play normal YouTube videos.\n\nMy environment data:\nOS:  Windows10 build 18312\nCPU: Intel Core i7-7820HK\nGPU: NVIDIA GTX 1070\nMem: 16G\nVRChat: Build 689, 2017.4.15.18523, 2017.4.15.6113371\nyoutube-dl: 2018.12.17.0",
